# Mode Study: A Dorian (repertoire plan: st-mode-dorian). An original 16-bar melody over a
# two-chord vamp: Am (x02210) for two bars, then D (xx0232) for two. The D major chord carries
# F#, the colour of Dorian: a minor scale with a bright sixth.
# The melody lands on F# on a strong beat in bars 3, 4, 8, 11, 12 and 15, over D, and passes
# through it over Am in bars 10 and 13, where it is the major sixth that makes Dorian. The last
# bars change faster (D in bar 15, Am in bar 16) so the tune can come home to A.
# Fifth position: finger 1 on fret 5, finger 3 on fret 7 (F# on string 2), finger 4 on fret 8.
# The same place on the neck as the Aeolian study: only F becomes F#.
title: Mode Study: A Dorian
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study on the Dorian mode
